1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,370
Listen, practice, speak. Practice makes you perfect.

2
00:00:12,370 --> 00:00:19,220
Hi everyone, thanks for joining us. If you're here to improve your English and succeed in

3
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:22,220
job interviews, you're in the right place.

4
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:27,100
That's right. Today we have a very important and practical topic that can really change

5
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:29,220
your career opportunities.

6
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:34,620
Absolutely. Today we're going to learn how to explain your work experience in a job

7
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:38,660
interview using clear and professional business English.

8
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:42,940
This is one of the most common and most important parts of any interview.

9
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:49,300
Yes, almost every interviewer will ask something like, can you tell me about your work experience?

10
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,420
And many people feel nervous because they don't know how to answer clearly.

11
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:54,740
Exactly.

12
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:59,220
Sometimes they have experience, but they can't explain it well in English.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:03,420
Or they give answers that are too short, too long, or not structured.

14
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:09,480
That's why today's episode will help you step by step with real examples, useful phrases,

15
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:11,800
and practice conversations.

16
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:12,800
Sounds great!

17
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:17,120
So before we begin, let me ask you, have you ever been nervous in a job interview?

18
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:22,540
Oh yes, many times, especially when I had to talk about my experience.

19
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:23,540
Same here.

20
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,800
It's one of the hardest parts because you want to sound confident and professional.

21
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:29,100
Exactly.

22
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:33,700
But the good news is, once you learn the structure, it becomes much easier.

23
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:36,220
Alright everyone, let's get started.

24
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:38,620
Let's begin with a simple question.

25
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:43,300
When an interviewer asks, tell me about your work experience, what are they really looking

26
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:44,300
for?

27
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:45,460
Great question!

28
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:48,040
They want to understand three main things.

29
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:52,460
What you did, what skills you have, and how you can help their company.

30
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:55,460
So it's not just about listing your jobs.

31
00:01:55,460 --> 00:01:56,460
Exactly.

32
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:59,800
about explaining your experience in a meaningful way.

33
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:02,680
So how should we start our answer?

34
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:07,400
A simple and effective way is to start with your current or most recent job.

35
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,960
Can you give an example?

36
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:14,640
Sure, you can say, I currently work as a marketing assistant at a digital agency.

37
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:16,640
That's clear and direct?

38
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:18,960
Yes, then you explain what you do.

39
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:21,000
Like your responsibilities?

40
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:21,880
Exactly.

41
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:28,000
For example, in my role, I manage social media accounts, create content, and analyze campaign

42
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,000
performance.

43
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,960
That sounds very professional.

44
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:37,480
Yes, and it's important to use action verbs, like manage, create, analyze, develop, and

45
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:38,480
coordinate.

46
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:39,840
Good point.

47
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:42,800
Action verbs make your experience sound stronger.

48
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:43,800
Exactly.

49
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:46,600
Now, let's build a complete answer together.

50
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:47,600
Okay.

51
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:49,040
Start with your job.

52
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:52,600
I currently work as a customer service representative.

53
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:55,240
Good. Now add responsibilities.

54
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:59,580
My main responsibilities include answering customer inquiries,

55
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:02,600
solving problems, and providing support.

56
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:05,160
Excellent. Now add an achievement.

57
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:09,560
I also improved customer satisfaction by 15%.

58
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:12,280
Perfect. That's a strong answer.

59
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:14,860
So achievements are important too.

60
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:18,880
Very important. They show results, not just tasks.

61
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:22,480
I see. Now let's talk about past experience.

62
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:27,520
Yes, if you had previous jobs, you can talk about them using the past tense.

63
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:29,020
Can you give an example?

64
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:34,800
Sure. Before this role, I worked as a sales assistant, where I helped customers and increased

65
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:35,800
sales.

66
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,200
That's simple and clear?

67
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:40,240
Yes. You don't need long sentences.

68
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:45,000
Now let's talk about structure. Is there a simple way to organize your answer?

69
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:49,760
Yes, a very useful method is present, past, and future.

70
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:51,160
That sounds interesting.

71
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:53,460
First, talk about your current job,

72
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:55,400
then your past experience.

73
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:57,880
Finally, connect it to the future.

74
00:03:57,880 --> 00:04:01,800
So you explain how your experience helps you in this job.

75
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:03,280
Exactly.

76
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,880
Let's try an example.

77
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:05,920
Go ahead.

78
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:08,840
I currently work as a project coordinator

79
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:12,480
where I manage timelines and communicate with clients.

80
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:14,920
Before this, I worked as an assistant

81
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:18,120
where I developed strong organizational skills.

82
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:22,000
I believe this experience will help me succeed in this role.

83
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,080
That's excellent, very clear and structured.

84
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:26,000
Thank you.

85
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,360
Now let's talk about a common mistake.

86
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:31,560
Many people just list their responsibilities.

87
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:35,220
Like saying I answer emails, I attend meetings,

88
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:36,720
I write reports.

89
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:39,320
Exactly, that's not enough detail.

90
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:41,160
So what should they do?

91
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:43,200
Add details and results.

92
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,960
explain how your work made a difference.

93
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:47,200
That makes sense.

94
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,960
Now let's do a role play.

95
00:04:48,960 --> 00:04:50,640
I'll be the interviewer.

96
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:52,040
Okay, I'm ready.

97
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:54,640
Can you tell me about your work experience?

98
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:55,920
Yes, of course.

99
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,400
I currently work as a software developer

100
00:04:58,400 --> 00:04:59,820
at a tech company.

101
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:03,360
My main responsibilities include developing applications,

102
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:06,320
fixing bugs and collaborating with my team.

103
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:09,420
In my previous role, I worked as a junior developer

104
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:11,080
where I learned programming skills

105
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,160
and improved system performance.

106
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:16,840
I believe my experience has prepared me well for this position.

107
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:18,480
That's a great answer.

108
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:19,360
Thank you.

109
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:23,080
Now let's talk about people with little or no experience.

110
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:25,980
Yes, students often worry about this.

111
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:28,040
If you don't have work experience,

112
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:31,840
you can talk about internships, projects, or studies.

113
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:33,400
Can you give an example?

114
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:36,600
I recently graduated, and during my studies,

115
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:38,480
I worked on several projects where

116
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:41,640
I developed teamwork and problem solving skills.

117
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:42,840
That's helpful.

118
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:46,560
You can also mention volunteer work or part-time jobs.

119
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:49,400
So everything counts as experience.

120
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:50,640
Exactly.

121
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:53,080
Now let's talk about confidence.

122
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:55,720
Yes, confidence is key.

123
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:57,940
Even if your English is not perfect,

124
00:05:57,940 --> 00:06:00,520
you should speak clearly and calmly.

125
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:03,080
And don't rush, take your time.

126
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:05,720
Now let's practice another role play.

127
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:06,840
Great idea.

128
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:08,400
You ask the question.

129
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:11,440
Okay, tell me about your work experience.

130
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:16,440
Yes, of course! I currently work as a software developer at a tech company.

131
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:23,440
My main responsibilities include developing applications, fixing bugs, and collaborating with my team.

132
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:30,440
In my previous role, I worked as a junior developer where I learned programming skills and improved system performance.

133
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:35,440
I believe my experience and skills make me a great fit for this position.

134
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:37,440
That's a great answer!

135
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:40,440
Thank you! Now let's talk about common mistakes.

136
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:43,440
Yes, very important.

137
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:46,880
Mistake number one, giving very short answers.

138
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:49,240
Like saying, I worked in sales.

139
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:52,160
Exactly, that's not enough detail.

140
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:55,720
Mistake number two, speaking too much without structure.

141
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:59,300
Yes, long and confusing answers.

142
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:03,040
Mistake number three, using incorrect grammar.

143
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:06,240
Especially mixing past tense and present tense.

144
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:09,800
Mistake number four, not giving examples.

145
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:14,920
support your answer with examples. Now let's do a longer role play.

146
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:15,920
Great idea.

147
00:07:15,920 --> 00:07:17,560
You're the interviewer again.

148
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:21,560
Okay. Can you describe your work experience in detail?

149
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:27,720
Certainly. I currently work as an operations assistant at a logistics company. My role

150
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:33,280
involves coordinating shipments, communicating with clients, and managing schedules. I

151
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:39,240
have improved efficiency by organizing workflows. Previously, I worked as an intern where

152
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:43,240
where I learned basic operations and developed teamwork skills.

153
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:49,240
Overall, my experience has helped me become organized, detail-oriented, and adaptable.

154
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:51,240
That's a very strong answer.

155
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:55,240
Thank you. Now let's talk about adding numbers.

156
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:56,240
Numbers?

157
00:07:56,240 --> 00:08:00,240
Yes, numbers make your experience more powerful.

158
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,240
Can you give an example?

159
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:07,240
I increased sales by 20%, or I managed a team of five people.

160
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:08,240
That sounds impressive.

161
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:13,240
Exactly. Numbers show real results. Now let's practice that.

162
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:14,240
Okay.

163
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:19,240
I handled over 50 customer calls per day and improved response time.

164
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,240
Perfect.

165
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:23,240
Now let's talk about ending your answer.

166
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:25,240
Yes, you should finish strong.

167
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:29,240
How? Connect your experience to the job.

168
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:34,240
Like saying, I believe my experience makes me a strong candidate for this position.

169
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:36,240
That's a great closing.

170
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:40,240
Now let's wrap everything into one final example.

171
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:41,240
Okay.

172
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:42,240
Go ahead.

173
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:48,240
I currently work as a financial analyst where I analyze data and prepare reports.

174
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:52,240
I have improved reporting accuracy by 25%.

175
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:57,240
Previously, I worked as an assistant where I developed strong analytical skills.

176
00:08:57,240 --> 00:09:02,240
I believe my experience and skills make me a great fit for this role.

177
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:04,240
That's an excellent answer.

178
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:05,240
Thank you.

179
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:07,240
Now let's summarize.

180
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:09,240
Start with your current job.

181
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:11,240
Explain your responsibilities.

182
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:13,240
Add achievements and results.

183
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:15,240
Talk about past experience.

184
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:17,240
Use clear structure.

185
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:20,240
And finish by connecting to the job.

186
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:23,240
Most importantly, be confident and clear.

187
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:26,240
Practice your answers before the interview.

188
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:28,240
Try speaking out loud.

189
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,240
Record yourself and listen.

190
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:32,240
Improve step by step.

191
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:34,240
Now it's your turn.

192
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:37,320
Practice explaining your work experience today.

193
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:39,960
Even if it's simple, start practicing.

194
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:42,160
Every small step helps.

195
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:44,360
Thank you so much for listening.

196
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:47,000
Keep practicing and stay confident.

197
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,040
We'll see you in the next episode.

198
00:09:49,040 --> 00:09:49,920
Goodbye.

199
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:52,560
We're really happy to have you with us today.

200
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:53,360
Hi, everyone.

201
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:54,720
Thanks for joining us.

202
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:57,600
If you're here to improve your English for job interviews,

203
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:59,880
you're definitely in the right place.

204
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:00,880
I'm Sarah.

205
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:02,200
And I'm Daniel.

206
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:08,640
On this podcast, we help you speak clear, confident business English in real life situations.

207
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:12,840
And today's topic is incredibly practical and important.

208
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:17,480
We're going to talk about how to explain your work experience in a job interview.

209
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:22,600
This is one of the most important skills you can have because honestly, in an interview,

210
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:26,920
this is where you either impress the interviewer or lose their attention.

211
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:27,920
Exactly.

212
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:31,920
You might have great experience, but if you don't explain it clearly, it won't

213
00:10:31,920 --> 00:10:36,320
help you. So today we're going to help you speak naturally, professionally, and

214
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:40,680
confidently when talking about your work experience. We'll give you real

215
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:45,360
examples, useful phrases, and we'll even practice full interview answers together.

216
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:51,120
Sounds great. So Sarah, before we begin, quick question, how are you today? I'm

217
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:55,160
doing really well. I actually had a mock interview session this morning with a

218
00:10:55,160 --> 00:11:00,040
student, so this topic feels very fresh. How about you? I'm great. I'm

219
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:04,000
I'm excited because this is something many learners struggle with, and today we're going

220
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,760
to make it much easier.

221
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:06,760
Absolutely.

222
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:09,320
Okay, everyone, let's get started.

223
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:14,880
So Sarah, let's begin with the most common interview question related to work experience.

224
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:17,120
Yes, the classic one.

225
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:19,880
Can you tell me about your work experience?

226
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:22,720
Simple question, but not a simple answer.

227
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:23,720
Exactly.

228
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:28,760
Many people make the mistake of giving either too little information or too much.

229
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:29,760
Right.

230
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:34,320
people just list jobs. I worked here, then here, then here.

231
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:38,020
And others tell their entire life story for 10 minutes.

232
00:11:38,020 --> 00:11:40,220
So what's the best approach?

233
00:11:40,220 --> 00:11:46,480
The best approach is structure. You need a clear, logical way to explain your experience.

234
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:49,560
Let's give a simple structure everyone can follow.

235
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:55,560
Yes, you can break it into three parts. Past, present, and key achievements.

236
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:57,320
That sounds easy to remember.

237
00:11:57,320 --> 00:12:03,520
It is. First, briefly talk about your past experience, then describe your current role,

238
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:06,400
and finally highlight your achievements and skills.

239
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:07,960
Let's give an example.

240
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:13,720
Sure. Here's a simple answer. I started my career as a sales assistant where I learned

241
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:19,360
how to communicate with customers and understand their needs. After that, I moved into a sales

242
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:26,320
executive role where I managed client accounts and increased sales by 20%. Currently, I work

243
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:31,560
as a sales manager, leading a team of five and developing sales strategies.

244
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:35,840
That's a great answer! It's clear, structured, and easy to follow.

245
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:39,440
And notice something important. It's not too long.

246
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:43,800
Yes, that's key. Interviews are conversations, not speeches.

247
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:48,840
Now let's talk about how to describe your responsibilities in your previous jobs.

248
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:51,960
This is where many learners struggle with vocabulary.

249
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:55,960
True, but the good news is, you don't need complicated words.

250
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:58,560
Simple, clear English is best.

251
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:04,160
So instead of trying to sound impressive with difficult words, focus on being clear.

252
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:05,260
Exactly.

253
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:09,760
For example, instead of saying something very complex, you can say,

254
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:14,360
I was responsible for managing customer inquiries and handling complaints.

255
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:18,760
Or I worked closely with the marketing team to develop campaigns.

256
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:22,360
Yes, let's give more examples for different roles.

257
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:26,120
If you're in customer service, I answered customer calls,

258
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:29,640
solved problems, and ensured customer satisfaction.

259
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:35,400
If you're in IT, I developed software applications and fixed technical issues.

260
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:38,680
If you're in administration, I organized meetings,

261
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:41,720
managed schedules, and prepared reports.

262
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:45,160
Notice how simple and clear these sentences are.

263
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:47,560
And they sound professional too.

264
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:50,440
Now let's move to something very important.

265
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:52,480
Talking about achievements.

266
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:56,040
Yes, this is where you really stand out in an interview.

267
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:57,160
Exactly.

268
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:59,800
Many candidates only talk about their duties,

269
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:01,840
but not their achievements.

270
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,400
So what's the difference?

271
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:06,120
Duties are what you were supposed to do.

272
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:09,000
Achievements are what you did successfully.

273
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,200
Ah, that's a big difference.

274
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:14,920
For example, duty, I managed a team.

275
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:19,920
Achievement, I managed a team and improved productivity by 30%.

276
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:22,000
That's much stronger.

277
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:26,240
Yes, numbers make your experience more powerful.

278
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,960
Let's give more examples.

279
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:32,120
I increased sales by 15% in six months.

280
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:36,240
I reduced customer complaints by improving service processes.

281
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:39,680
I completed a project two weeks ahead of schedule.

282
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:42,920
These are the kind of statements interviewers love.

283
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:47,320
Now let's talk about a very useful technique, the STAR method.

284
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:51,780
Yes, this is extremely helpful for explaining experience clearly.

285
00:14:51,780 --> 00:14:57,140
STAR stands for Situation, Task, Action, and Result.

286
00:14:57,140 --> 00:14:58,340
Let's break it down.

287
00:14:58,340 --> 00:15:01,260
Situation, describe the context.

288
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:04,000
Task, explain your responsibility.

289
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,280
Action, say what you did.

290
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:08,800
Result, explain the outcome.

291
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:10,820
Let's give a full example.

292
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:11,720
Sure.

293
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:17,560
In my previous job, we were facing a decline in customer satisfaction situation.

294
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:21,440
My task was to improve the service quality, task.

295
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:26,160
I introduced a new feedback system and trained the team, action.

296
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:31,640
As a result, customer satisfaction increased by 25% result.

297
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:33,480
That's an excellent answer.

298
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:36,400
It's structured, clear, and impactful.

299
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:39,080
Now, Sarah, let's talk about a common problem.

300
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:42,080
What if someone doesn't have much experience?

301
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:43,080
Good question.

302
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:47,080
This happens a lot, especially for students or fresh graduates.

303
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:48,840
So what can they say?

304
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:52,560
They can talk about internships, projects, volunteering,

305
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:54,400
or even academic work.

306
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:57,820
So experience doesn't have to be a full-time job?

307
00:15:57,820 --> 00:15:58,880
Exactly.

308
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:01,240
Any relevant experience counts.

309
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:02,560
Give us an example.

310
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:05,000
During my studies, I completed a project

311
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:08,160
where I worked in a team to develop a marketing plan.

312
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:11,440
I was responsible for research and presentation.

313
00:16:11,440 --> 00:16:12,920
That sounds professional.

314
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:17,100
Yes, and it shows skills like teamwork and communication.

315
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:21,280
Now let's talk about common mistakes when explaining work experience.

316
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:24,320
Yes, this is very important.

317
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:26,960
Mistake number one, being too vague.

318
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:31,640
For example, I did many things or I helped the team.

319
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:33,920
That doesn't tell the interviewer anything.

320
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:35,940
Instead, be specific.

321
00:16:35,940 --> 00:16:40,860
I helped the team by organizing weekly meetings and tracking progress.

322
00:16:40,860 --> 00:16:41,860
Much better.

323
00:16:41,860 --> 00:16:45,740
Mistake number two, using incorrect verb tenses.

324
00:16:45,740 --> 00:16:48,160
Ah yes, very common.

325
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:50,580
Use past tense for previous jobs.

326
00:16:50,580 --> 00:16:53,940
I worked, I managed, I developed.

327
00:16:53,940 --> 00:16:56,060
And present tense for your current role.

328
00:16:56,060 --> 00:16:58,820
I manage, I lead, I create.

329
00:16:58,820 --> 00:17:00,220
Exactly.

330
00:17:00,220 --> 00:17:03,860
Mistake number three, speaking too fast or too much.

331
00:17:03,860 --> 00:17:08,260
Yes, some candidates get nervous and start talking non-stop.

332
00:17:08,260 --> 00:17:11,500
Remember, clarity is more important than speed.

333
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:12,460
Take your time.

334
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:14,020
Speak clearly.

335
00:17:14,020 --> 00:17:17,340
OK, Sarah, I think it's time for a full role play.

336
00:17:17,340 --> 00:17:20,100
Yes, this will help everyone understand how

337
00:17:20,100 --> 00:17:22,260
to use everything we discussed.

338
00:17:22,260 --> 00:17:25,020
I'll be the interviewer, and you'll be the candidate.

339
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:25,780
Perfect.

340
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:26,860
Let's begin.

341
00:17:26,860 --> 00:17:27,580
Good morning.

342
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:30,060
Can you tell me about your work experience?

343
00:17:30,060 --> 00:17:30,820
Good morning.

344
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:32,500
Thank you for the opportunity.

345
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:35,740
I have over five years of experience in marketing.

346
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:38,340
I started my career as a marketing assistant

347
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:42,060
where I supported campaigns and conducted market research.

348
00:17:42,060 --> 00:17:44,820
After that, I became a marketing executive

349
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:48,740
where I managed social media accounts and created content.

350
00:17:48,740 --> 00:17:51,340
Currently, I work as a marketing manager

351
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:55,100
leading a team of five and developing sales strategies.

352
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:56,660
That's a strong answer.

353
00:17:56,660 --> 00:17:59,380
Can you describe one of your key achievements?

354
00:17:59,380 --> 00:18:00,340
Certainly.

355
00:18:00,340 --> 00:18:06,340
In my current role, I led a campaign that increased our online engagement by 40%.

356
00:18:06,340 --> 00:18:12,260
I worked closely with my team to create targeted content and analyze customer behavior.

357
00:18:12,260 --> 00:18:16,140
As a result, we saw significant growth in brand awareness.

358
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:17,260
Excellent.

359
00:18:17,260 --> 00:18:20,580
What were your main responsibilities in your previous role?

360
00:18:20,580 --> 00:18:25,660
In my previous role, I was responsible for managing social media platforms, creating

361
00:18:25,660 --> 00:18:28,340
content, and analyzing performance.

362
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:32,820
I also collaborated with the design team to develop marketing materials.

363
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:34,660
Very clear. Thank you.

364
00:18:34,660 --> 00:18:35,540
Thank you.

365
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:37,460
That was a great example.

366
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:41,700
Yes, and notice how the answers were structured and specific.

367
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:43,140
And not too long.

368
00:18:43,140 --> 00:18:44,340
Exactly.

369
00:18:44,340 --> 00:18:49,300
Now let's do another quick role play, but this time with the beginner level candidates.

370
00:18:49,300 --> 00:18:50,420
Great idea.

371
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:51,220
Ready?

372
00:18:51,220 --> 00:18:51,940
Ready.

373
00:18:51,940 --> 00:18:54,340
Can you tell me about your work experience?

374
00:18:54,340 --> 00:18:58,820
I recently graduated so I don't have full-time work experience yet.

375
00:18:58,820 --> 00:19:05,140
However, I completed an internship where I assisted with administrative tasks and customer service.

376
00:19:05,140 --> 00:19:09,940
I also worked on a team project at university where we developed a business plan.

377
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:11,700
That's a very good answer.

378
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:13,860
Yes, simple but effective.

379
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:16,580
Now let's wrap up with some final advice.

380
00:19:16,580 --> 00:19:20,260
Sure. First, always structure your answer.

381
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:23,460
Second, be specific and give examples.

382
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:27,140
Third, highlight achievements, not just duties.

383
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:29,060
And finally, practice.

384
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:31,700
Practice is the key to confidence.

385
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:33,260
Now it's your turn.

386
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:35,300
Try answering this question.

387
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:37,860
Can you tell me about your work experience?

388
00:19:37,860 --> 00:19:38,940
Say it out loud.

389
00:19:38,940 --> 00:19:40,860
Practice like a real interview.

390
00:19:40,860 --> 00:19:43,260
You can even record yourself and listen.

391
00:19:43,260 --> 00:19:45,100
That's a great way to improve.

392
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:48,420
Before we finish, we want to say thank you for listening.

393
00:19:48,420 --> 00:19:50,460
Your support means a lot to us.

394
00:19:50,460 --> 00:19:52,620
Keep practicing, keep improving,

395
00:19:52,620 --> 00:19:55,180
and don't be afraid of interviews.

396
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:56,540
You can do this.

397
00:19:56,540 --> 00:19:57,940
See you in the next episode.

398
00:19:57,940 --> 00:19:59,140
Goodbye, everyone.

399
00:19:59,140 --> 00:20:00,140
Hello.

400
00:20:00,140 --> 00:20:01,740
Welcome back to English Talk.

401
00:20:01,740 --> 00:20:03,820
We're really happy to have you with us today.

402
00:20:03,820 --> 00:20:05,020
Hi, everyone.

403
00:20:05,020 --> 00:20:06,300
Thanks for joining us.

404
00:20:06,300 --> 00:20:09,700
If you're here to improve your English, you're in the right place.

405
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:10,900
I'm Emily.

406
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,340
And I'm Jack.

407
00:20:12,340 --> 00:20:17,780
On this channel, we help you speak clear, natural English with confidence in real life

408
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:18,980
situations.

409
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:23,740
If you enjoyed this lesson, please give us a thumbs up, and don't forget to subscribe.

410
00:20:23,740 --> 00:20:27,000
Yes, your support helps us so much.

411
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,540
Thank you for being here.

412
00:20:28,540 --> 00:20:31,700
So Emily, what are we talking about today?

413
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:35,220
Today we have a very practical and important topic.

414
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:39,420
We're going to learn how to explain your work experience in a job interview.

415
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:42,120
Oh, this is such an important skill.

416
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:44,780
I think many people struggle with this.

417
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:45,940
Absolutely.

418
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:50,740
Many learners know English, but they don't know how to explain their experience clearly

419
00:20:50,740 --> 00:20:52,300
and confidently.

420
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:54,780
And interviews can be stressful, too.

421
00:20:54,780 --> 00:20:59,580
Yes, especially when you're trying to speak in English and make a good impression at the

422
00:20:59,580 --> 00:21:00,580
same time.

423
00:21:00,580 --> 00:21:04,380
So, today we're going to make it simple and practical.

424
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:05,380
Exactly.

425
00:21:05,380 --> 00:21:12,780
We'll teach useful phrases, give real examples, show common mistakes, and do practice conversations.

426
00:21:12,780 --> 00:21:14,180
Sounds perfect.

427
00:21:14,180 --> 00:21:16,340
Before we start, how are you feeling today?

428
00:21:16,340 --> 00:21:17,660
I'm feeling great!

429
00:21:17,660 --> 00:21:22,180
I'm excited because this lesson can really help people succeed in interviews.

430
00:21:22,180 --> 00:21:23,180
How about you?

431
00:21:23,180 --> 00:21:24,620
I'm feeling good too.

432
00:21:24,620 --> 00:21:26,420
Ready to help everyone improve.

433
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:27,420
Great!

434
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:28,420
Let's get started.

435
00:21:28,420 --> 00:21:32,380
So, Emily, let's begin with a common interview question.

436
00:21:32,380 --> 00:21:38,380
Yes, one of the most common questions is, can you tell me about your work experience?

437
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:42,660
That question sounds simple, but it can be difficult to answer.

438
00:21:42,660 --> 00:21:43,820
Exactly.

439
00:21:43,820 --> 00:21:46,860
Many people don't know how to organize their answer.

440
00:21:46,860 --> 00:21:48,580
So what should we do?

441
00:21:48,580 --> 00:21:53,820
You should follow a simple structure, past, present, and results.

442
00:21:53,820 --> 00:21:55,060
That sounds easy.

443
00:21:55,060 --> 00:21:56,500
Can you explain it?

444
00:21:56,500 --> 00:21:57,500
Yes.

445
00:21:57,500 --> 00:22:02,060
First, talk about your past experience, then describe your current role.

446
00:22:02,060 --> 00:22:05,460
Finally, mention your achievements or results.

447
00:22:05,460 --> 00:22:07,180
Let's start with the past.

448
00:22:07,180 --> 00:22:08,420
What should we say?

449
00:22:08,420 --> 00:22:12,540
You can begin with something like, I started my career as…

450
00:22:12,540 --> 00:22:13,540
Example?

451
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:16,180
I started my career as a sales assistant

452
00:22:16,180 --> 00:22:17,620
in a retail company.

453
00:22:17,620 --> 00:22:18,780
That's clear.

454
00:22:18,780 --> 00:22:20,460
Yes, and simple.

455
00:22:20,460 --> 00:22:22,820
What if I have more experience?

456
00:22:22,820 --> 00:22:25,740
You can add, then I moved on to.

457
00:22:25,740 --> 00:22:26,780
Example?

458
00:22:26,780 --> 00:22:29,180
Then I moved on to a marketing role

459
00:22:29,180 --> 00:22:31,940
where I managed social media campaigns.

460
00:22:31,940 --> 00:22:33,980
That sounds very professional.

461
00:22:33,980 --> 00:22:35,140
Exactly.

462
00:22:35,140 --> 00:22:37,420
Now let's talk about the present.

463
00:22:37,420 --> 00:22:40,180
In this part, you describe your current job.

464
00:22:40,180 --> 00:22:41,460
What should we say?

465
00:22:41,460 --> 00:22:43,340
Currently, I work as.

466
00:22:43,340 --> 00:22:48,420
For example, currently, I work as a project manager at a tech company.

467
00:22:48,420 --> 00:22:50,820
And then we explain responsibilities.

468
00:22:50,820 --> 00:22:51,820
Yes.

469
00:22:51,820 --> 00:22:57,700
For example, I am responsible for managing clients and delivering projects on time.

470
00:22:57,700 --> 00:22:59,220
That's very clear.

471
00:22:59,220 --> 00:23:00,220
Exactly.

472
00:23:00,220 --> 00:23:03,060
Now the most important part, results.

473
00:23:03,060 --> 00:23:04,060
Yes.

474
00:23:04,060 --> 00:23:06,300
This is where you show your value.

475
00:23:06,300 --> 00:23:08,460
What do you mean by results?

476
00:23:08,460 --> 00:23:11,980
Achievements, improvements, or success stories.

477
00:23:11,980 --> 00:23:13,500
Can you give an example?

478
00:23:13,500 --> 00:23:17,660
I helped increase sales by 20% in six months.

479
00:23:17,660 --> 00:23:19,060
That sounds impressive.

480
00:23:19,060 --> 00:23:22,220
Yes, numbers make your answers stronger.

481
00:23:22,220 --> 00:23:26,700
So instead of saying, I did a good job, we should be specific.

482
00:23:26,700 --> 00:23:27,700
Exactly.

483
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:30,420
Now, let's put everything together.

484
00:23:30,420 --> 00:23:31,420
Great idea.

485
00:23:31,420 --> 00:23:34,780
I started as a customer service representative.

486
00:23:34,780 --> 00:23:39,340
Then I moved on to a team leader role where I supervised five people.

487
00:23:39,340 --> 00:23:42,620
Currently, I work as a customer service manager.

488
00:23:42,620 --> 00:23:47,300
I am responsible for handling client issues and improving service quality.

489
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:51,180
I helped reduce customer complaints by 30%.

490
00:23:51,180 --> 00:23:52,740
That's a perfect answer.

491
00:23:52,740 --> 00:23:55,180
It sounds natural and professional.

492
00:23:55,180 --> 00:23:57,660
Yes, and easy to remember.

493
00:23:57,660 --> 00:24:00,340
Now let's talk about common mistakes.

494
00:24:00,340 --> 00:24:01,660
Good idea.

495
00:24:01,660 --> 00:24:02,900
Mistake number one.

496
00:24:02,900 --> 00:24:04,780
Speaking too generally.

497
00:24:04,780 --> 00:24:05,780
Example?

498
00:24:05,780 --> 00:24:08,980
I worked in a company and did many things.

499
00:24:08,980 --> 00:24:10,300
That's not clear.

500
00:24:10,300 --> 00:24:11,420
Exactly.

501
00:24:11,420 --> 00:24:13,660
You need to give details.

502
00:24:13,660 --> 00:24:15,260
Mistake number two.

503
00:24:15,260 --> 00:24:17,540
Talking too much without structure.

504
00:24:17,540 --> 00:24:20,300
So the interviewer gets confused.

505
00:24:20,300 --> 00:24:21,460
Yes.

506
00:24:21,460 --> 00:24:23,700
Always organize your answer.

507
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:25,380
Mistake number three.

508
00:24:25,380 --> 00:24:27,540
Using incorrect tense.

509
00:24:27,540 --> 00:24:31,340
Past for previous jobs, present for current job?

510
00:24:31,340 --> 00:24:32,460
Exactly.

511
00:24:32,460 --> 00:24:34,020
Mistake number four.

512
00:24:34,020 --> 00:24:35,700
Being too negative.

513
00:24:35,700 --> 00:24:38,340
Like complaining about past jobs?

514
00:24:38,340 --> 00:24:41,080
Yes, always stay positive.

515
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:43,160
Now let's do a role play.

516
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:43,920
Great.

517
00:24:43,920 --> 00:24:46,640
Can you tell me about your work experience?

518
00:24:46,640 --> 00:24:49,840
Yes, I started as a junior accountant.

519
00:24:49,840 --> 00:24:50,520
Good.

520
00:24:50,520 --> 00:24:51,400
Continue.

521
00:24:51,400 --> 00:24:53,680
Then I worked as a senior accountant

522
00:24:53,680 --> 00:24:55,920
where I handled financial reports.

523
00:24:55,920 --> 00:24:56,680
Nice.

524
00:24:56,680 --> 00:24:58,960
Currently, I am a finance manager.

525
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:01,200
I manage a team of five people.

526
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:02,200
Excellent.

527
00:25:02,200 --> 00:25:03,520
Add results.

528
00:25:03,520 --> 00:25:07,080
I improved reporting efficiency by 25%.

529
00:25:07,080 --> 00:25:14,660
perfect answer. Thank you. Let's try a bad example. Okay. I worked in many jobs. I did

530
00:25:14,660 --> 00:25:22,660
a lot of tasks. That's too vague. Yes, not good. Let me improve it. Go ahead. I started

531
00:25:22,660 --> 00:25:29,420
as an assistant. Then I became a coordinator. Now I work as a manager. Much better. Let's

532
00:25:29,420 --> 00:25:31,020
Let's add more detail.

533
00:25:31,020 --> 00:25:32,020
Yes.

534
00:25:32,020 --> 00:25:35,420
I manage projects and coordinate teams.

535
00:25:35,420 --> 00:25:36,420
Excellent improvement.

536
00:25:36,420 --> 00:25:38,820
Now, let's talk about confidence.

537
00:25:38,820 --> 00:25:41,820
Yes, this is very important.

538
00:25:41,820 --> 00:25:44,700
Confidence comes from preparation and practice.

539
00:25:44,700 --> 00:25:48,060
So we should practice our answers before the interview.

540
00:25:48,060 --> 00:25:49,220
Exactly.

541
00:25:49,220 --> 00:25:51,420
You can practice in front of a mirror.

542
00:25:51,420 --> 00:25:52,660
Or with a friend.

543
00:25:52,660 --> 00:25:53,660
Yes.

544
00:25:53,660 --> 00:25:56,380
Now let's do a longer role-play interview.

545
00:25:56,380 --> 00:25:57,380
Perfect.

546
00:25:57,380 --> 00:25:58,380
Good morning.

547
00:25:58,380 --> 00:26:00,660
tell me about your work experience?

548
00:26:00,660 --> 00:26:05,540
Good morning. Thank you for the opportunity. I started as a marketing assistant.

549
00:26:05,540 --> 00:26:06,340
Go on.

550
00:26:06,340 --> 00:26:10,300
In that role, I supported campaigns and created content.

551
00:26:10,300 --> 00:26:11,620
Good detail.

552
00:26:11,620 --> 00:26:16,700
Then I became a marketing executive where I managed social media accounts.

553
00:26:16,700 --> 00:26:17,580
Nice.

554
00:26:17,580 --> 00:26:22,260
Currently, I am a marketing manager. I lead a team and plan strategies.

555
00:26:22,260 --> 00:26:23,380
Excellent.

556
00:26:23,380 --> 00:26:27,620
I increased online engagement by 40% in one year.

557
00:26:27,620 --> 00:26:29,220
That's a strong answer.

558
00:26:29,220 --> 00:26:30,020
Thank you.

559
00:26:30,020 --> 00:26:32,740
Let's talk about another common question.

560
00:26:32,740 --> 00:26:35,700
Yes, what are your key responsibilities?

561
00:26:35,700 --> 00:26:37,220
How do we answer that?

562
00:26:37,220 --> 00:26:40,980
Use simple sentences like, I am responsible for.

563
00:26:40,980 --> 00:26:41,940
Example?

564
00:26:41,940 --> 00:26:46,100
I am responsible for managing clients and preparing reports.

565
00:26:46,100 --> 00:26:47,220
Very clear.

566
00:26:47,220 --> 00:26:50,180
Another question is, what did you achieve?

567
00:26:50,180 --> 00:26:52,100
That's about results.

568
00:26:52,100 --> 00:26:55,140
Yes, you can say, I successfully.

569
00:26:55,140 --> 00:26:56,100
Example?

570
00:26:56,100 --> 00:26:59,620
I successfully completed a project ahead of schedule.

571
00:26:59,620 --> 00:27:01,060
That sounds great!

572
00:27:01,060 --> 00:27:03,860
Now, let's do one more full example.

573
00:27:03,860 --> 00:27:04,660
Okay.

574
00:27:04,660 --> 00:27:07,140
I started as a software developer.

575
00:27:07,140 --> 00:27:07,860
Then?

576
00:27:07,860 --> 00:27:11,940
I worked on multiple projects and improved system performance.

577
00:27:11,940 --> 00:27:12,740
Good.

578
00:27:12,740 --> 00:27:16,180
I am currently a senior developer leading a team.

579
00:27:16,180 --> 00:27:16,980
Nice.

580
00:27:16,980 --> 00:27:20,180
I reduced system errors by 50%.

581
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:21,620
Excellent answer.

582
00:27:21,620 --> 00:27:22,420
Thank you.

583
00:27:22,420 --> 00:27:26,740
Today we learned how to explain work experience in a job interview.

584
00:27:26,740 --> 00:27:32,020
We covered structure, useful phrases, mistakes, and practice examples.

585
00:27:32,020 --> 00:27:35,860
The key is to be clear, structured, and confident.

586
00:27:35,860 --> 00:27:39,300
Yes, and use real examples with results.

587
00:27:39,300 --> 00:27:40,980
Practice regularly.

588
00:27:40,980 --> 00:27:43,700
And keep your English simple and natural.

589
00:27:43,700 --> 00:27:46,260
Thank you everyone for joining us today.

590
00:27:46,260 --> 00:27:48,740
Keep practicing and we'll see you next time.

591
00:27:48,740 --> 00:27:49,780
Bye everyone.

592
00:27:49,780 --> 00:27:50,780
Goodbye!

593
00:27:50,780 --> 00:27:53,340
We're really happy to have you with us today.

594
00:27:53,340 --> 00:27:54,340
Hi everyone!

595
00:27:54,340 --> 00:27:55,660
Thanks for joining us.

596
00:27:55,660 --> 00:28:00,500
If you're here to improve your English for job interviews, you're in the right place.

597
00:28:00,500 --> 00:28:01,820
I'm Emily.

598
00:28:01,820 --> 00:28:02,980
And I'm Jack.

599
00:28:02,980 --> 00:28:07,220
And today we're going to help you master one of the most important parts of any

600
00:28:07,220 --> 00:28:08,220
interview.

601
00:28:08,220 --> 00:28:12,700
Yes, today's topic is incredibly practical and powerful.

602
00:28:12,700 --> 00:28:17,580
We're going to talk about how to explain your work experience in a job interview.

603
00:28:17,580 --> 00:28:23,460
This is a game-changer, because honestly, it doesn't matter how much experience you have

604
00:28:23,460 --> 00:28:25,900
if you can't explain it clearly.

605
00:28:25,900 --> 00:28:26,900
Exactly.

606
00:28:26,900 --> 00:28:31,840
You might have amazing skills, but if you struggle to describe them, the interviewer may not

607
00:28:31,840 --> 00:28:33,920
see your true value.

608
00:28:33,920 --> 00:28:39,160
So today, we'll teach you how to explain your experience step by step, using simple

609
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:40,860
and natural English.

610
00:28:40,860 --> 00:28:46,140
We'll also share real examples, common mistakes, and practice conversations so

611
00:28:46,140 --> 00:28:48,940
so you can feel confident in your next interview.

612
00:28:48,940 --> 00:28:50,100
Sounds great.

613
00:28:50,100 --> 00:28:54,060
So Emily, before we begin, how are you feeling today?

614
00:28:54,060 --> 00:28:55,220
I'm feeling great.

615
00:28:55,220 --> 00:28:56,820
I'm excited because this topic

616
00:28:56,820 --> 00:28:59,340
can really help people get better jobs.

617
00:28:59,340 --> 00:29:00,500
What about you?

618
00:29:00,500 --> 00:29:01,380
Same here.

619
00:29:01,380 --> 00:29:03,540
I think this is one of the most useful lessons

620
00:29:03,540 --> 00:29:05,060
we've ever done.

621
00:29:05,060 --> 00:29:07,420
All right, everyone, let's get started.

622
00:29:07,420 --> 00:29:09,180
Okay, Emily, let's begin

623
00:29:09,180 --> 00:29:12,260
with a very common interview question.

624
00:29:12,260 --> 00:29:14,220
You mean the classic one?

625
00:29:14,220 --> 00:29:17,820
Yes, can you tell me about your work experience?

626
00:29:17,820 --> 00:29:22,340
Ah, yes, this question comes up in almost every interview.

627
00:29:22,340 --> 00:29:25,740
And many people don't know how to answer it properly.

628
00:29:25,740 --> 00:29:29,340
They either say too little or too much.

629
00:29:29,340 --> 00:29:30,340
Exactly.

630
00:29:30,340 --> 00:29:32,020
So, let's break it down.

631
00:29:32,020 --> 00:29:36,340
When you answer this question, you should follow a simple structure.

632
00:29:36,340 --> 00:29:37,900
Structure is key.

633
00:29:37,900 --> 00:29:40,980
Without structure, your answer can sound confusing.

634
00:29:40,980 --> 00:29:41,980
Right.

635
00:29:41,980 --> 00:29:46,700
Basic structure is past, present, and key achievements.

636
00:29:46,700 --> 00:29:48,540
Let's explain that clearly.

637
00:29:48,540 --> 00:29:51,900
First, you talk about your past experience,

638
00:29:51,900 --> 00:29:55,780
then you talk about your current job or most recent role,

639
00:29:55,780 --> 00:29:59,740
and finally, you highlight your achievements or skills.

640
00:29:59,740 --> 00:30:00,900
Let's give an example.

641
00:30:00,900 --> 00:30:02,220
I'll go first.

642
00:30:02,220 --> 00:30:03,420
Go ahead.

643
00:30:03,420 --> 00:30:06,700
I started my career as a customer service assistant

644
00:30:06,700 --> 00:30:09,580
where I helped customers and handled complaints.

645
00:30:09,580 --> 00:30:15,260
After two years, I moved into a sales role, where I developed strong communication skills.

646
00:30:15,260 --> 00:30:21,420
Currently, I work as a sales executive, and I've increased sales by 20% in the past year.

647
00:30:21,420 --> 00:30:23,420
That's a perfect answer.

648
00:30:23,420 --> 00:30:26,980
It's clear, structured, and includes results.

649
00:30:26,980 --> 00:30:31,060
Yes, and notice I didn't use very complicated words.

650
00:30:31,060 --> 00:30:32,460
That's important.

651
00:30:32,460 --> 00:30:35,300
Simple English is often more effective.

652
00:30:35,300 --> 00:30:37,740
Now, let's talk about something important.

653
00:30:37,740 --> 00:30:40,540
Many people just list their jobs.

654
00:30:40,540 --> 00:30:46,040
Yes, like, I worked here, then I worked there, then I worked somewhere else.

655
00:30:46,040 --> 00:30:48,240
Exactly. That's not enough.

656
00:30:48,240 --> 00:30:52,040
You need to explain what you did and what you achieved.

657
00:30:52,040 --> 00:30:56,640
So instead of saying, I worked in marketing, you should say something like,

658
00:30:56,640 --> 00:31:02,340
I worked in marketing where I managed social media campaigns and increased engagement.

659
00:31:02,340 --> 00:31:03,240
Perfect.

660
00:31:03,240 --> 00:31:06,040
Always add action and results.

661
00:31:06,040 --> 00:31:08,580
Let's talk about useful phrases.

662
00:31:08,580 --> 00:31:10,480
Emily, can you give us some?

663
00:31:10,480 --> 00:31:12,440
Sure, you can start with,

664
00:31:12,440 --> 00:31:15,960
I have X years of experience in,

665
00:31:15,960 --> 00:31:17,760
that's a great opening.

666
00:31:17,760 --> 00:31:19,120
You can also say,

667
00:31:19,120 --> 00:31:20,560
in my previous role,

668
00:31:20,560 --> 00:31:22,860
I was responsible for,

669
00:31:22,860 --> 00:31:25,700
very common and very useful.

670
00:31:25,700 --> 00:31:26,960
Another one is,

671
00:31:26,960 --> 00:31:29,300
I worked closely with,

672
00:31:29,300 --> 00:31:31,160
that shows teamwork.

673
00:31:31,160 --> 00:31:35,140
And one of my main achievements was,

674
00:31:35,140 --> 00:31:38,100
That's powerful. It shows results.

675
00:31:38,100 --> 00:31:40,660
Let's build a full answer together.

676
00:31:40,660 --> 00:31:42,740
Okay, I'll try. Go ahead.

677
00:31:43,460 --> 00:31:47,140
I have three years of experience in digital marketing.

678
00:31:47,140 --> 00:31:52,420
In my previous role, I managed social media accounts and created content.

679
00:31:52,420 --> 00:31:56,900
I worked closely with the design team to improve our brand image.

680
00:31:56,900 --> 00:32:01,380
One of my main achievements was increasing our online engagement by 30%.

681
00:32:01,380 --> 00:32:02,380
percent.

682
00:32:02,380 --> 00:32:03,380
Excellent.

683
00:32:03,380 --> 00:32:06,140
That's a strong and professional answer.

684
00:32:06,140 --> 00:32:07,140
Thanks.

685
00:32:07,140 --> 00:32:10,500
Now, let's talk about another common question.

686
00:32:10,500 --> 00:32:13,580
You mean, what did you do in your last job?

687
00:32:13,580 --> 00:32:15,440
Yes, exactly.

688
00:32:15,440 --> 00:32:20,100
This question is similar but more focused on your most recent experience.

689
00:32:20,100 --> 00:32:22,540
So you should go into more detail.

690
00:32:22,540 --> 00:32:23,540
Right.

691
00:32:23,540 --> 00:32:27,780
Talk about your daily tasks, responsibilities, and impact.

692
00:32:27,780 --> 00:32:29,740
Let's give a practical example.

693
00:32:29,740 --> 00:32:30,740
Okay?

694
00:32:30,740 --> 00:32:34,500
In my last job, I worked as an administrative assistant.

695
00:32:34,500 --> 00:32:39,660
My main responsibilities included managing emails, scheduling meetings, and preparing

696
00:32:39,660 --> 00:32:40,660
reports.

697
00:32:40,660 --> 00:32:46,260
I also supported the team by organizing documents and improving office processes.

698
00:32:46,260 --> 00:32:48,460
That's very clear.

699
00:32:48,460 --> 00:32:51,660
But we can make it even better by adding results.

700
00:32:51,660 --> 00:32:55,100
Yes, always add results if possible.

701
00:32:55,100 --> 00:33:01,340
So we can say, I also helped improve office efficiency by organizing documents and creating

702
00:33:01,340 --> 00:33:03,260
a new filing system.

703
00:33:03,260 --> 00:33:04,260
Perfect!

704
00:33:04,260 --> 00:33:05,860
Now it sounds more impressive.

705
00:33:05,860 --> 00:33:09,140
Now, let's talk about something beginners.

706
00:33:09,140 --> 00:33:12,420
What if someone doesn't have much work experience?

707
00:33:12,420 --> 00:33:13,420
Good question.

708
00:33:13,420 --> 00:33:18,900
In that case, you can talk about internships, projects, or even school experience.

709
00:33:18,900 --> 00:33:22,540
So experience doesn't have to be a full-time job.

710
00:33:22,540 --> 00:33:23,540
Exactly.

711
00:33:23,540 --> 00:33:28,920
For example, I recently graduated and during my studies I worked on several group projects

712
00:33:28,920 --> 00:33:32,660
where I developed teamwork and communication skills.

713
00:33:32,660 --> 00:33:35,080
That's a great way to show potential.

714
00:33:35,080 --> 00:33:37,060
You can also mention volunteering.

715
00:33:37,060 --> 00:33:43,380
Yes, like I volunteered at a local organization where I helped organize events and manage

716
00:33:43,380 --> 00:33:45,060
social media.

717
00:33:45,060 --> 00:33:46,780
That's valuable experience.

718
00:33:46,780 --> 00:33:51,220
Now, let's talk about something very important, storytelling.

719
00:33:51,220 --> 00:33:56,900
Ah, yes, interviews are not just about facts, they're about stories.

720
00:33:56,900 --> 00:33:58,300
Exactly.

721
00:33:58,300 --> 00:34:01,020
People remember stories more than lists.

722
00:34:01,020 --> 00:34:05,820
So instead of just saying what you did, tell a short story about a situation.

723
00:34:05,820 --> 00:34:06,900
Okay.

724
00:34:06,900 --> 00:34:10,940
In my previous role, we had a problem with customer complaints.

725
00:34:10,940 --> 00:34:16,460
I took the initiative to analyze the feedback and suggested changes to our process.

726
00:34:16,460 --> 00:34:20,860
As a result, customer satisfaction improved significantly.

727
00:34:20,860 --> 00:34:21,920
It's a great story.

728
00:34:21,920 --> 00:34:24,460
It shows problem-solving skills.

729
00:34:24,460 --> 00:34:25,960
And initiative.

730
00:34:25,960 --> 00:34:27,460
And results.

731
00:34:27,460 --> 00:34:28,660
Exactly.

732
00:34:28,660 --> 00:34:31,180
Now let's practice a full interview answer.

733
00:34:31,180 --> 00:34:32,700
I'll be the interviewer.

734
00:34:32,700 --> 00:34:34,500
Okay, I'm ready.

735
00:34:34,500 --> 00:34:36,980
Can you tell me about your work experience?

736
00:34:36,980 --> 00:34:37,980
Sure.

737
00:34:37,980 --> 00:34:41,420
I have five years of experience in customer service.

738
00:34:41,420 --> 00:34:46,940
I started as a customer support assistant where I handled inquiries and solved customer

739
00:34:46,940 --> 00:34:48,240
issues.

740
00:34:48,240 --> 00:34:53,860
After two years, I was promoted to team leader where I managed a team of five people.

741
00:34:53,860 --> 00:34:59,240
In my current role, I focus on improving customer satisfaction, and I've successfully reduced

742
00:34:59,240 --> 00:35:02,040
complaint response time by 40%.

743
00:35:02,040 --> 00:35:03,040
Excellent.

744
00:35:03,040 --> 00:35:05,240
That's a very strong answer.

745
00:35:05,240 --> 00:35:06,240
Thanks.

746
00:35:06,240 --> 00:35:08,880
Now, let's improve it even more.

747
00:35:08,880 --> 00:35:10,600
Add a personal touch.

748
00:35:10,600 --> 00:35:11,600
Okay?

749
00:35:11,600 --> 00:35:16,440
I really enjoy helping customers and finding solutions to their problems.

750
00:35:16,440 --> 00:35:17,440
Perfect.

751
00:35:17,440 --> 00:35:19,040
It shows personality.

752
00:35:19,040 --> 00:35:22,200
Now, let's talk about common mistakes.

753
00:35:22,200 --> 00:35:25,140
Yes, this is very important.

754
00:35:25,140 --> 00:35:28,240
Mistake number one, being too vague.

755
00:35:28,240 --> 00:35:31,480
For example, I did many things.

756
00:35:31,480 --> 00:35:34,480
That doesn't tell the interviewer anything.

757
00:35:34,480 --> 00:35:36,480
Always be specific.

758
00:35:36,480 --> 00:35:40,280
Mistake number two, using too many technical words.

759
00:35:40,280 --> 00:35:44,320
Yes, especially if the interviewer may not understand them.

760
00:35:44,320 --> 00:35:47,220
Keep your language simple and clear.

761
00:35:47,220 --> 00:35:50,780
Mistake number three, not mentioning results.

762
00:35:50,780 --> 00:35:52,860
This is a big one.

763
00:35:52,860 --> 00:35:56,060
Always try to include numbers or outcomes.

764
00:35:56,060 --> 00:36:01,380
Like increased sales, reduced costs, or improved efficiency.

765
00:36:01,380 --> 00:36:04,300
Mistake number four, speaking too long.

766
00:36:04,300 --> 00:36:07,580
Yes, don't give a ten minute answer.

767
00:36:07,580 --> 00:36:09,860
Keep it concise but meaningful.

768
00:36:09,860 --> 00:36:12,180
Now let's do another role play.

769
00:36:12,180 --> 00:36:13,380
Great idea.

770
00:36:13,380 --> 00:36:15,420
This time I'll be the interviewer.

771
00:36:15,420 --> 00:36:17,180
Okay, I'm ready.

772
00:36:17,180 --> 00:36:20,500
Can you describe your previous work experience?

773
00:36:20,500 --> 00:36:25,020
Of course, I have four years of experience in project management.

774
00:36:25,020 --> 00:36:30,380
In my previous role, I managed multiple projects and coordinated with different teams.

775
00:36:30,380 --> 00:36:35,900
I was responsible for planning timelines, allocating resources, and ensuring projects

776
00:36:35,900 --> 00:36:37,960
were completed on time.

777
00:36:37,960 --> 00:36:42,980
One of my key achievements was successfully delivering a major project two weeks ahead

778
00:36:42,980 --> 00:36:43,980
of schedule.

779
00:36:43,980 --> 00:36:45,920
That's excellent.

780
00:36:45,920 --> 00:36:46,920
Thank you.

781
00:36:46,920 --> 00:36:49,920
Notice how clear and confident that sounded.

782
00:36:49,920 --> 00:36:52,720
Yes, confidence is very important.

783
00:36:52,720 --> 00:36:57,120
Even if your English is not perfect, confidence makes a big difference.

784
00:36:57,120 --> 00:36:58,600
Absolutely.

785
00:36:58,600 --> 00:37:01,800
Now let's do one more example, for beginners.

786
00:37:01,800 --> 00:37:02,800
Okay?

787
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:07,720
I don't have much work experience yet, but I recently completed an internship where

788
00:37:07,720 --> 00:37:10,000
I assisted with marketing tasks.

789
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:14,440
I helped create content and learned how to manage social media accounts.

790
00:37:14,440 --> 00:37:17,940
I'm eager to learn and develop my skills further.

791
00:37:17,940 --> 00:37:20,400
That's a great answer for someone starting out.

792
00:37:20,400 --> 00:37:23,360
Yes, it shows willingness to learn.

793
00:37:23,360 --> 00:37:26,280
Now let's wrap up with some final advice.

794
00:37:26,280 --> 00:37:30,680
First, always prepare your answer before the interview.

795
00:37:30,680 --> 00:37:32,440
Practice speaking out loud.

796
00:37:32,440 --> 00:37:35,880
Second, use simple and clear English.

797
00:37:35,880 --> 00:37:40,240
Third, focus on your achievements, not just your duties.

798
00:37:40,240 --> 00:37:43,480
And finally, be confident and natural.

799
00:37:43,480 --> 00:37:46,080
Remember, your experience is valuable.

800
00:37:46,080 --> 00:37:48,400
You just need to explain it well.

801
00:37:48,400 --> 00:37:49,400
Exactly.

802
00:37:49,400 --> 00:37:51,400
Now, it's your turn.

803
00:37:51,400 --> 00:37:53,760
Think about your own work experience.

804
00:37:53,760 --> 00:37:56,120
How would you describe it in English?

805
00:37:56,120 --> 00:37:58,640
Try using the structure we taught today.

806
00:37:58,640 --> 00:38:02,060
Write it down, practice it, and say it out loud.

807
00:38:02,060 --> 00:38:05,400
The more you practice, the more confident you'll become.

808
00:38:05,400 --> 00:38:08,200
And confidence is key in any interview.

809
00:38:08,200 --> 00:38:11,040
Alright, everyone, that's all for today.

810
00:38:11,040 --> 00:38:12,960
Thank you so much for listening.

811
00:38:12,960 --> 00:38:16,240
Keep practicing, keep learning, and don't give up.

812
00:38:16,240 --> 00:38:18,640
We'll see you in the next episode.

813
00:38:18,640 --> 00:38:19,640
Goodbye everyone.

814
00:38:19,640 --> 00:38:20,640
Goodbye.

815
00:38:20,640 --> 00:38:27,320
We're really happy to have you with us today.

816
00:38:27,320 --> 00:38:28,320
Hi everyone.

817
00:38:28,320 --> 00:38:29,800
Thanks for joining us.

818
00:38:29,800 --> 00:38:33,960
If you're here to improve your English for job interviews, you're absolutely in the

819
00:38:33,960 --> 00:38:34,960
right place.

820
00:38:34,960 --> 00:38:35,960
I'm Emily.

821
00:38:35,960 --> 00:38:37,080
And I'm Jack.

822
00:38:37,080 --> 00:38:42,440
And on this channel, we help you speak clear, confident, and natural English in real

823
00:38:42,440 --> 00:38:44,760
life professional situations.

824
00:38:44,760 --> 00:38:47,640
If you enjoy this lesson, don't forget to support us.

825
00:38:47,640 --> 00:38:50,680
Yes, your support means a lot to us.

826
00:38:50,680 --> 00:38:53,360
So Emily, what are we talking about today?

827
00:38:53,360 --> 00:38:56,720
Today's topic is extremely important and practical.

828
00:38:56,720 --> 00:39:01,040
We're going to learn how to explain your work experience in a job interview.

829
00:39:01,040 --> 00:39:02,040
That's a big one.

830
00:39:02,040 --> 00:39:05,200
I think many people feel nervous about this question.

831
00:39:05,200 --> 00:39:06,200
Absolutely.

832
00:39:06,200 --> 00:39:10,520
When an interviewer says, tell me about your work experience, many people don't know

833
00:39:10,520 --> 00:39:12,000
where to start.

834
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:14,960
Or they talk too much, or too little.

835
00:39:14,960 --> 00:39:15,960
Exactly!

836
00:39:15,960 --> 00:39:21,300
So today, we'll show you how to answer clearly, professionally, and confidently, with lots

837
00:39:21,300 --> 00:39:23,200
of practical examples.

838
00:39:23,200 --> 00:39:28,240
And we'll also practice together so you can use these phrases in your own interviews.

839
00:39:28,240 --> 00:39:29,240
Perfect!

840
00:39:29,240 --> 00:39:32,320
So, Jack, before we begin, how are you feeling today?

841
00:39:32,320 --> 00:39:33,320
I'm feeling great!

842
00:39:33,320 --> 00:39:37,800
I'm excited because this topic can really help people succeed in interviews.

843
00:39:37,800 --> 00:39:38,800
How about you?

844
00:39:38,800 --> 00:39:39,800
I feel the same.

845
00:39:39,800 --> 00:39:41,880
I think this lesson will be very useful.

846
00:39:41,880 --> 00:39:43,880
Great! So, let's get started!

847
00:39:43,880 --> 00:39:47,880
Okay, let's begin with the most common interview request.

848
00:39:47,880 --> 00:39:50,380
Can you tell me about your work experience?

849
00:39:50,380 --> 00:39:54,880
Right. This question is almost guaranteed in every interview.

850
00:39:54,880 --> 00:39:59,380
Yes, and your answer needs structure. You can't just speak randomly.

851
00:39:59,380 --> 00:40:01,880
So, what's the best way to structure it?

852
00:40:01,880 --> 00:40:06,880
A simple and effective structure is past, present, and key achievements.

853
00:40:06,880 --> 00:40:09,880
That sounds easy. Can you explain it?

854
00:40:09,880 --> 00:40:15,960
Of course, first talk about your past experience, what you did before, then explain your current

855
00:40:15,960 --> 00:40:16,960
role.

856
00:40:16,960 --> 00:40:19,640
Finally, highlight your achievements or results.

857
00:40:19,640 --> 00:40:23,640
So, it's like telling a short story about your career.

858
00:40:23,640 --> 00:40:24,640
Exactly!

859
00:40:24,640 --> 00:40:26,120
Let me give you an example.

860
00:40:26,120 --> 00:40:31,520
I started my career as a sales assistant, where I developed strong communication skills.

861
00:40:31,520 --> 00:40:36,200
After that, I worked as a sales executive for three years, managing client accounts

862
00:40:36,200 --> 00:40:37,960
and increasing revenue.

863
00:40:37,960 --> 00:40:42,260
Currently, I am a sales manager leading a team of five people.

864
00:40:42,260 --> 00:40:47,320
One of my key achievements was increasing sales by 20% in one year.

865
00:40:47,320 --> 00:40:49,600
That sounds very clear and professional.

866
00:40:49,600 --> 00:40:53,160
Yes, and notice it's not too long and not too short.

867
00:40:53,160 --> 00:40:54,160
I like that.

868
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:56,640
It shows progress and results.

869
00:40:56,640 --> 00:41:00,440
Now Emily, what if someone has very little experience?

870
00:41:00,440 --> 00:41:02,720
Maybe they are a student or a beginner.

871
00:41:02,720 --> 00:41:03,720
Good question.

872
00:41:03,720 --> 00:41:08,720
In that case, they can talk about internships, projects, or even volunteer work.

873
00:41:08,720 --> 00:41:12,720
So, experience doesn't always mean a full-time job.

874
00:41:12,720 --> 00:41:14,720
Exactly. Let me give an example.

875
00:41:14,720 --> 00:41:18,720
I recently graduated with a degree in business administration.

876
00:41:18,720 --> 00:41:22,720
During my studies, I completed an internship at a marketing company

877
00:41:22,720 --> 00:41:25,720
where I assisted with social media campaigns.

878
00:41:25,720 --> 00:41:28,720
I also worked on a group project where we developed a business plan.

879
00:41:28,720 --> 00:41:32,720
These experiences helped me build teamwork and communication skills.

880
00:41:32,720 --> 00:41:36,720
That's great. It still shows skills and effort.

881
00:41:36,720 --> 00:41:40,720
Yes, employers care about skills, not just job titles.

882
00:41:40,720 --> 00:41:45,720
Now let's talk about an important detail. Many people just list their responsibilities.

883
00:41:45,720 --> 00:41:48,720
Yes, and that's a common mistake.

884
00:41:48,720 --> 00:41:49,720
Why is that a problem?

885
00:41:49,720 --> 00:41:54,720
Because responsibilities don't show impact. You need to talk about results.

886
00:41:54,720 --> 00:42:00,720
Ah, so instead of saying, I answered emails, you should say something stronger.

887
00:42:00,720 --> 00:42:06,000
Exactly. For example, instead of I answered customer emails, say,

888
00:42:06,000 --> 00:42:10,800
I handled customer inquiries and improved response time by 30%.

889
00:42:10,800 --> 00:42:12,960
That sounds much more impressive.

890
00:42:12,960 --> 00:42:15,200
Yes, because it shows value.

891
00:42:15,200 --> 00:42:19,440
Let's practice transforming weak answers into strong ones.

892
00:42:19,440 --> 00:42:23,360
Great idea! I'll give a weak sentence, you improve it.

893
00:42:23,360 --> 00:42:24,880
Okay, I'm ready.

894
00:42:24,880 --> 00:42:27,040
I worked in customer service.

895
00:42:27,040 --> 00:42:34,540
Hmm, I worked in customer service where I handled client issues and improved customer satisfaction.

896
00:42:34,540 --> 00:42:37,040
Very good. Now add a result.

897
00:42:37,040 --> 00:42:43,540
I worked in customer service where I handled client issues and helped increase customer satisfaction ratings.

898
00:42:43,540 --> 00:42:46,540
Perfect. That's exactly what interviewers want.

899
00:42:46,540 --> 00:42:50,040
Now let's talk about useful phrases you can use.

900
00:42:50,040 --> 00:42:53,540
Yes, phrases make your answer sound more natural.

901
00:42:53,540 --> 00:42:55,540
Here are some great starters.

902
00:42:55,540 --> 00:42:58,660
I have over three years of experience in...

903
00:42:58,660 --> 00:43:00,460
I have a background in...

904
00:43:00,460 --> 00:43:02,420
I previously worked as...

905
00:43:02,420 --> 00:43:04,620
In my current role, I...

906
00:43:04,620 --> 00:43:07,380
One of my main responsibilities is...

907
00:43:07,380 --> 00:43:09,820
One of my key achievements was...

908
00:43:09,820 --> 00:43:13,300
These phrases help you sound fluent and confident.

909
00:43:13,300 --> 00:43:14,940
And they're easy to remember.

910
00:43:14,940 --> 00:43:17,660
Now let's create a full example together.

911
00:43:17,660 --> 00:43:21,020
Great! Imagine you're applying for a marketing job.

912
00:43:21,020 --> 00:43:22,860
Okay. Let me try.

913
00:43:22,860 --> 00:43:26,360
I have over four years of experience in marketing.

914
00:43:26,360 --> 00:43:31,660
I started as a marketing assistant where I supported campaigns and managed social media

915
00:43:31,660 --> 00:43:32,660
accounts.

916
00:43:32,660 --> 00:43:37,980
After that, I became a marketing executive where I planned campaigns and worked closely

917
00:43:37,980 --> 00:43:38,980
with clients.

918
00:43:38,980 --> 00:43:44,020
Currently, I'm a marketing specialist focusing on digital strategy.

919
00:43:44,020 --> 00:43:49,220
One of my key achievements was increasing website traffic by 40%.

920
00:43:49,220 --> 00:43:52,060
That's excellent, very clear and structured.

921
00:43:52,060 --> 00:43:54,060
Thank you. I followed the formula.

922
00:43:54,060 --> 00:43:56,060
Yes, and it works perfectly.

923
00:43:56,060 --> 00:44:00,060
Now let's talk about another important skill, being specific.

924
00:44:00,060 --> 00:44:02,060
What do you mean by specific?

925
00:44:02,060 --> 00:44:05,060
Use numbers, examples, and details.

926
00:44:05,060 --> 00:44:12,060
So instead of saying, I improved sales, say, I increased sales by 15%.

927
00:44:12,060 --> 00:44:16,060
Exactly. Numbers make your answers stronger and more believable.

928
00:44:16,060 --> 00:44:20,060
That makes sense. What about people who change careers?

929
00:44:20,060 --> 00:44:24,060
Good question. They should connect their past experience to the new role.

930
00:44:24,060 --> 00:44:26,060
Can you give an example?

931
00:44:26,060 --> 00:44:33,060
Sure. I previously worked in customer service where I developed strong communication and problem-solving skills.

932
00:44:33,060 --> 00:44:39,060
I'm now transitioning into sales where I can use these skills to build relationships with clients.

933
00:44:39,060 --> 00:44:41,060
That's smart. It shows relevance.

934
00:44:41,060 --> 00:44:45,060
Yes. Always connect your experience to the job.

935
00:44:45,060 --> 00:44:47,060
Now let's do a role-play interview.

936
00:44:47,060 --> 00:44:50,660
Great idea! You be the candidate, I'll be the interviewer.

937
00:44:50,660 --> 00:44:51,500
Ready.

938
00:44:51,500 --> 00:44:53,940
Can you tell me about your work experience?

939
00:44:53,940 --> 00:44:55,140
Yes, of course.

940
00:44:55,140 --> 00:44:58,500
I have over five years of experience in finance.

941
00:44:58,500 --> 00:45:00,540
I started as a junior analyst

942
00:45:00,540 --> 00:45:03,980
where I supported senior staff with data analysis.

943
00:45:03,980 --> 00:45:06,780
After that, I worked as a financial analyst,

944
00:45:06,780 --> 00:45:09,820
managing reports and forecasting budgets.

945
00:45:09,820 --> 00:45:13,580
Currently, I'm a senior analyst, leading a team of three.

946
00:45:13,580 --> 00:45:15,260
One of my key achievements

947
00:45:15,260 --> 00:45:19,020
was improving reporting efficiency by 25%.

948
00:45:19,020 --> 00:45:21,260
Excellent, that's a strong answer.

949
00:45:21,260 --> 00:45:23,500
Now let's improve it even more.

950
00:45:23,500 --> 00:45:24,300
Really?

951
00:45:24,300 --> 00:45:26,660
Yes, add a personal touch.

952
00:45:26,660 --> 00:45:29,340
Okay, I enjoy working with data

953
00:45:29,340 --> 00:45:31,260
in solving complex problems,

954
00:45:31,260 --> 00:45:33,500
which is why I've grown in this field.

955
00:45:33,500 --> 00:45:35,860
Perfect, that adds personality.

956
00:45:35,860 --> 00:45:38,180
Let's talk about common mistakes.

957
00:45:38,180 --> 00:45:40,520
Yes, this is very important.

958
00:45:40,520 --> 00:45:43,580
Mistake one, speaking too generally.

959
00:45:43,580 --> 00:45:46,340
like saying I did many tasks.

960
00:45:46,340 --> 00:45:48,620
Exactly, be specific.

961
00:45:48,620 --> 00:45:51,920
Mistake two, using incorrect tense.

962
00:45:51,920 --> 00:45:55,220
So, past jobs equals past tense.

963
00:45:55,220 --> 00:45:58,740
Correct, and current job equals present tense.

964
00:45:58,740 --> 00:46:01,580
Mistake three, speaking too long.

965
00:46:01,580 --> 00:46:03,980
Don't tell your whole life story.

966
00:46:03,980 --> 00:46:06,880
Exactly, keep it clear and focused.

967
00:46:06,880 --> 00:46:09,480
Now let's do a longer role play interview.

968
00:46:09,480 --> 00:46:10,980
Great, I'll start.

969
00:46:10,980 --> 00:46:13,220
Can you describe your work experience?

970
00:46:13,220 --> 00:46:17,500
Yes, I have over six years of experience in project management.

971
00:46:17,500 --> 00:46:23,140
I began as a project assistant, where I supported project planning and coordination.

972
00:46:23,140 --> 00:46:29,660
After that, I became a project coordinator, managing timelines and communication between teams.

973
00:46:29,660 --> 00:46:35,940
Currently, I'm a project manager, leading multiple projects and ensuring they are delivered on time.

974
00:46:35,940 --> 00:46:41,740
One of my key achievements was successfully completing a project two weeks ahead of schedule.

975
00:46:41,740 --> 00:46:44,260
That's excellent, very professional.

976
00:46:44,260 --> 00:46:46,220
Let's add a follow-up question.

977
00:46:46,220 --> 00:46:47,060
Okay.

978
00:46:47,060 --> 00:46:49,980
What skills did you develop in your previous roles?

979
00:46:49,980 --> 00:46:52,220
I developed strong organizational

980
00:46:52,220 --> 00:46:53,860
and communication skills.

981
00:46:53,860 --> 00:46:56,820
I also improved my ability to manage deadlines

982
00:46:56,820 --> 00:46:58,180
and work under pressure.

983
00:46:58,180 --> 00:46:59,380
Great answer.

984
00:46:59,380 --> 00:47:01,060
This is really helpful.

985
00:47:01,060 --> 00:47:03,260
Yes, and practice is the key.

986
00:47:03,260 --> 00:47:05,980
Let's give one final full example.

987
00:47:05,980 --> 00:47:06,860
Go ahead.

988
00:47:06,860 --> 00:47:10,740
I have over three years of experience in IT support.

989
00:47:10,740 --> 00:47:15,940
I started as a junior technician where I helped resolve basic technical issues.

990
00:47:15,940 --> 00:47:21,860
Later, I worked as an IT support specialist, handling more complex problems and supporting

991
00:47:21,860 --> 00:47:23,340
clients remotely.

992
00:47:23,340 --> 00:47:29,060
Currently, I'm a senior support engineer where I lead a small team and manage critical

993
00:47:29,060 --> 00:47:30,060
issues.

994
00:47:30,060 --> 00:47:34,820
One of my key achievements was reducing system downtime by 30 percent.

995
00:47:34,820 --> 00:47:36,380
That's fantastic!

996
00:47:36,380 --> 00:47:38,820
Clear, structured, and impactful.

997
00:47:38,820 --> 00:47:40,700
Okay, let's wrap up.

998
00:47:40,700 --> 00:47:42,500
We covered a lot today.

999
00:47:42,500 --> 00:47:44,660
We learned how to structure your answer.

1000
00:47:44,660 --> 00:47:47,140
Past, present, and achievements.

1001
00:47:47,140 --> 00:47:49,080
We learned to be specific.

1002
00:47:49,080 --> 00:47:51,060
Use numbers and examples.

1003
00:47:51,060 --> 00:47:53,780
We practiced real interview answers.

1004
00:47:53,780 --> 00:47:56,020
And we corrected common mistakes.

1005
00:47:56,020 --> 00:47:58,740
The most important thing is confidence.

1006
00:47:58,740 --> 00:48:00,240
And preparation.

1007
00:48:00,240 --> 00:48:02,500
Practice your answer before the interview.

1008
00:48:02,500 --> 00:48:04,180
Say it out loud.

1009
00:48:04,180 --> 00:48:05,780
Record yourself if possible.

1010
00:48:05,780 --> 00:48:07,780
And improve step by step.

1011
00:48:07,780 --> 00:48:09,220
Now it's your turn.

1012
00:48:09,220 --> 00:48:11,220
Try answering this question.

1013
00:48:11,220 --> 00:48:14,220
Can you tell me about your work experience?

1014
00:48:14,220 --> 00:48:16,140
Write your answer and practice it.

1015
00:48:16,140 --> 00:48:18,020
Keep it clear and simple.

1016
00:48:18,020 --> 00:48:20,100
Thank you so much for joining us today.

1017
00:48:20,100 --> 00:48:23,340
We hope this lesson helps you succeed in your interviews.

1018
00:48:23,340 --> 00:48:24,940
Keep practicing your English.

1019
00:48:24,940 --> 00:48:27,060
And keep improving every day.

1020
00:48:27,060 --> 00:48:28,660
We'll see you in the next lesson.

1021
00:48:28,660 --> 00:48:29,420
Goodbye, everyone.
